    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneV_13.3/p@199963",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "RICHARD.\nMy noble father,\nThree times today I holp him to his horse,\nThree times bestrid him; thrice I led him off,\nPersuaded him from any further act;\nBut still, where danger was, still there I met him,\nAnd like rich hangings in a homely house,\nSo was his will in his old feeble body.\nBut, noble as he is, look where he comes.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
