      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneV_13.3/p@200509",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "SALISBURY.\nBy th’ mass, so did we all. I thank you, Richard.\nGod knows how long it is I have to live,\nAnd it hath pleased him that three times today\nYou have defended me from imminent death.\nWell, lords, we have not got that which we have;\n’Tis not enough our foes are this time fled,\nBeing opposites of such repairing nature.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneV_13.3/p@200509/line-1",
          "start": 0,
